habit|regular-behaviour|NOUN|regular way of behaving|Something you do repeatedly, often without thinking carefully about it.|thói quen|Checking the gate before bed became a habit for my grandfather.|Việc kiểm tra cổng trước khi ngủ trở thành thói quen của ông tôi.|Countable: a habit of doing something; get into or break a habit.|0
illegal|against-the-law|ADJECTIVE|against the law|Not allowed by the law that applies in a place.|bất hợp pháp; trái pháp luật|The fictional detective investigated an illegal trade in stolen artworks.|Vị thám tử trong truyện điều tra hoạt động buôn bán trái phép những tác phẩm nghệ thuật bị đánh cắp.|Illegal activity; it is illegal to do something. Lawfulness depends on the applicable law.|0
outdoor|outside-buildings|ADJECTIVE|taking place outside|Taking place or used outside buildings.|ngoài trời|The school moved its outdoor concert to the covered courtyard.|Nhà trường chuyển buổi hòa nhạc ngoài trời sang sân có mái che.|Usually before a noun: outdoor activities. Outdoors is the adverb: play outdoors.|0
sometimes|on-some-occasions|ADVERB|on some occasions|On some occasions, but not every time.|đôi khi; thỉnh thoảng|My neighbour sometimes brings fresh herbs from her garden.|Người hàng xóm đôi khi mang rau thơm tươi từ vườn nhà đến.|Usually before a main verb and after be; also possible at the beginning or end. Not some times meaning several occasions.|0
winding|having-many-bends|ADJECTIVE|having many bends|Following a route with many curves or turns.|quanh co; uốn lượn|We followed a winding path between the tea fields.|Chúng tôi đi theo một lối mòn quanh co giữa những đồi chè.|Winding road or path; pronounced with the vowel of find, unlike wind meaning moving air.|-
